# Note

## Summary
A freeform written record, usually about something. Deliberately small: `title`, markdown `body`, `author` (links User), `createdAt` (the shared Created At block), and the link that gives a note its power — `about`, the card it annotates (`linksTo(CardDef)`, so a note can attach to anything). The card title falls back to a cleaned excerpt of the body, so untitled quick notes still list legibly; embedded and fitted formats lead with the excerpt.

## Why it exists
content-calendar recorded the gap directly on the tracker: there was no Note CardDef to extend, so ContentIdea extended CardDef and the finding sat in the concept's notes. This block closes it — the extension surface is the point.

## Usage
```ts
import Note from './note';

export class SessionNote extends Note {
  static displayName = 'Session Note';
  @field session = linksTo(() => Session);
}
```
The linked example is a real coordination note (the Template-row discrepancy) attached via `about` to the MatrixConcept card it concerns.

## Non-goals
Not a message: no recipient, no thread, no visibility flag — the ticket-message FieldDef the crawl once matched here is a different concept and stays with tickets. Not a document: no sections, no attachments (Document is its own layer-05 row). Editing history is the platform's, not the card's.
